==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|festif}}, from {{der|en|la|festivus|t=pertaining to a feast, gay, lively, joyous}}. Equivalent to {{affix|en|feast|-ive}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-festive.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having the [[atmosphere]], [[decoration]], or [[attitude]] of a [[festival]], [[holiday]], or [[celebration]].
#: {{ux|en|The room was decked out in '''festive''' streamers, with flowers everywhere.}}
# In the mood to [[celebrate]].
#: {{ux|en|Please put the Christmas decorations away, I'm really not in a '''festive''' mood.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|feastful}}
* {{l|en|feastly}}

